& [RawDictationSet] preserves the governing user language without replacing prior snapshots
  + [text_1] is "this will coordinate around a local utility which will operate the database to find the files that address the meaning based on database correlation weights for the input terms to associate them with the intended purpose SOP files that declare forms and features and functions accessible from there"
  + [text_2] is "then I'm thinking the neural net representing the SOP layout should resolve it's correlations to the file name and line number that governs a given perspective. then the program that serves as the SOP director will take input, resolve the SOP meaning, and quote those file lines"
  + [text_3] is "Cantor only reads files that have been compiled to it's source reading (neural net) and have the digital signature recognized at compile time. updated files must be recompiled. Cantor cannot authorize any terms, propositions, conditions, or any instruction from a file without a recognized signature CRC."
  + [text_4] is "a neural-net association of terms, directives and conditions, scoped for purpose, and the program that hashes and searches that hash for the signed entry"
  + [text_5] is "so I'm imagining that Cantor is a database query engine... it queries the table of SOP by association, and it returns the relationships, the records, the proof."
  + [text_6] is "so I'm thinking that the SOP system should then be ordered by identity, the table of proper nouns and their descriptions, relationships, intended purposes, etc. and the files that correspond to those names. this should be just like a table of contents. then a table for \"index\" as a file that describe verbs with their constraints, pointing towards their applicable identities as referenced in the table of contents. then you need a scanning tool that correlates and weaves between these two structures as it plans an objective"

& [CurrentTurnRefinement] preserves the selected interpretation
  + [identity_catalogue] is the table-of-contents view of stable subjects meanings purposes boundaries relations and signed source addresses
  + [operation_catalogue] is the index view of verbs operations roles inputs outputs conditions constraints and applicable identity families
  + [association] may rank which exact records deserve inspection under a subject purpose and use case
  + [authority] remains exact signed package admission and cannot be manufactured by association weight
  + [bridge] should carry selected semantic addresses into the existing proof-carrying query and later attention-procedure surfaces
  + [first_manifestation] should be deterministic provider-free and fixture-bounded before any learned router is trained or admitted

